  "question": {
    "text": "In a LCR circuit capacitance is changed from $C$ to $2 C$. For the resonant frequency to remain unchanged, the inductance should be changed from $L$ to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TtWw0",
      "text": "\n$4 \\mathrm{~L}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vhUzL",
      "text": "\n$2 \\mathrm{~L}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oWdAY",
      "text": "\nL/2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "aUBYK",
      "text": "\nL/4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\omega_{\\text {res }}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{L C}}\n$$\nif $\\omega_{\\text {res }}$ is to remain same, the product LC should also not change.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{LC}=\\mathrm{L}^{\\prime} \\mathrm{C}^{\\prime} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{LC}=\\mathrm{L}^{\\prime} 2 \\mathrm{C} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{L}^{\\prime}=\\mathrm{L}^2 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
